    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Changes:\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**\n- Renamed the stored `customer_code`/`customerCode` field to `member_id`/`memberId` with `getMemberId()`/`setMemberId()`.\n- Removed the derived `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()` getters.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `customerCode(owner)` with `memberId(owner)`, which builds `<REGION>` (locality) + `<FY>` (2-digit fiscal year from `getFiscalYear()`) + `<HASH8>` (first-8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`, unchanged from the region-and-hash identity) + `<CHK>` (a Luhn digit over the decimal digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`, via a new `luhnCheckDigit` helper). Collision handling now dedups against existing `memberId`s.\n- `primaryIdentifier(owner)` now returns `getMemberId()`, so the audit record references the memberId.\n- Human audit line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` (JSON key now `memberId`) carry the memberId.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added the `memberId` property (`fiscalYear` retained).\n\n**`resources/db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(40)` to accommodate the longer id).\n\nThe behavioral changes the spec called out are all in place: collision handling applies to the `memberId`, the fiscal-year value is embedded within it, `fiscalYear` output stays an `FY<YY>` field, `ownerSegment` is unchanged, and both the human and structured audit records now carry the `memberId`.",
